<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 17 November, from 1558 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1558</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth I becomes queen of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of her half-sister Mary I, the 25-year-old Elizabeth succeeded to the throne. Her 44-year reign brought a Protestant church settlement, the defeat of the Spanish Armada and a flowering of literature.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1869</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Suez Canal opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Empress Eugénie of France led a procession of ships through the new canal linking the Mediterranean and the Red Sea. It cut thousands of kilometres from the sea route between Europe and Asia.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1970</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luna 17 lands Lunokhod 1 on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet Luna 17 landed in the Sea of Rains and released Lunokhod 1, the first remote-controlled rover on another world. Driven from Earth, it travelled about 10 kilometres over ten months.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1973</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Greek troops crush the Athens Polytechnic uprising</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A tank broke through the gates of the Athens Polytechnic, ending a student occupation against the military junta. Dozens were killed, and the junta fell the following summer.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1989</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Police attack students in Prague, sparking the Velvet Revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Riot police beat students at a Prague march marking the anniversary of a Nazi crackdown. Outrage fuelled mass protests that ended communist rule in Czechoslovakia within six weeks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></li></ol>
